                <pb facs="0371" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p2/pg861"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/2–1548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Cuba </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-17T17:00:00-05:00">February 17,
                            1948—5 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>226. For Clayton from Lovett. Senate Foreign Relations Committee has approved
                    provision in ERP legislation requiring inclusion in bilateral agreements of a
                    commitment that participating countries (which include western Germany) must
                    cooperate with each other in stimulating interchange of goods and reducing trade
                    barriers among themselves. You may advise ERP countries that we would expect
                    clause such as you suggest ur 196 Feb 15 in bilatetal ERP agreements, as part of
                    implementation this policy. You may also advise Chinese Del that we would expect
                    similar provision in China aid bilateral agreement. [Lovett.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
